    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89-a3">

                <pb facs="0188" n="80" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg80"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3, in No.
                    94.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Diplomatic corps to the Minister of Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The ministers of England, Portugal, Italy, the United States of America, and the
                    chargé d’affaires of France have the honor to inform his excellency the minister
                    of foreign affairs that the commanding officers of the foreign naval forces in
                    the bay of Rio de Janeiro having examined the complaints made on the 8th instant
                    to the dean of the diplomatic corps are of the opinion that the fire directed
                    upon the city of Rio de Janeiro by Fort Villegaignon and by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aquidaban</hi> with machine guns was provoked by the
                    incessant firing of inexperienced troops stationed along the shore of the
                    city.</p>
                <p>The commanders are fully of the opinion that under the circumstances it would not
                    be appropriate to communicate with Admiral de Mello in order to remind him of
                    his engagements.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
